I reviewed the render and the write-up together. My verdict follows.

{
  "verdict": "return",
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "reasons": [
    {
      "criterion": "loads",
      "met": true,
      "note": "The page rendered with plenty of visible content and a 200."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "core-path-named",
      "met": false,
      "note": "'Vendors can manage their bookings' is a description of a feature, not a path.
Write it as the numbered steps a stranger follows: open the link, pick a date, choose a vendor, pay the token amount."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "core-path-works",
      "met": false,
      "note": "The render shows a landing page with a waitlist form and no way into a product. There is no entry point to the path you describe."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "no-placeholders",
      "met": true,
      "note": "No lorem text on what the render did show."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "serves-the-job",
      "met": true,
      "note": "What you describe is the wedding-vendor product from checkpoint 1."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "honest-gaps",
      "met": true,
      "note": "The gaps you list are specific."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "overall-quality",
      "met": false,
      "note": "Overall this is closer to a landing page than a product."
    }
  ],
  "rubricScores": {
    "loads": 82,
    "core-path-named": 24,
    "core-path-works": 6,
    "no-placeholders": 74,
    "serves-the-job": 70,
    "honest-gaps": 71,
    "overall-quality": 30
  },
  "contradictions": [],
  "flags": [],
  "summaryForStudent": "The page loads, but what loads is a waitlist, not the product. Ship the booking flow you describe, name the path as numbered steps, and send it again."
}

Happy to look again once the booking flow is live.
